# MediCitas — versioned request collection (VS Code "REST Client" format; the JetBrains HTTP client
# understands the same requests). The command-line demo is demo/demo.mjs; this file is for exploring
# the API by hand.
#
# Passwords are NOT stored here: they are read from the environment of the editor process. Start the
# editor from a shell where .env is exported, e.g.  set -a; . ./.env; set +a; code .
# Seeded logins: docs/data/seed-data.md. Contract: docs/contracts/api-contracts.md.

@gateway = http://localhost:8000
@keycloak = http://localhost:8080
@professionalId = 42000000-0000-4000-8000-000000010001
@serviceId = 41000000-0000-4000-8000-000000010001
@date = 2026-12-01

### 1. Token of a receptionist of clinic 1 (Keycloak issues every token)
# @name receptionistLogin
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/medicitas/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=medicitas-cli&username=carlos.jimenez@sanjose.medicitas.test&password={{$processEnv MEDICITAS_DEMO_USER_PASSWORD}}

### 2. Token of the clinic-1 administrator
# @name adminLogin
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/medicitas/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=medicitas-cli&username=ana.mora@sanjose.medicitas.test&password={{$processEnv MEDICITAS_DEMO_USER_PASSWORD}}

### 3. Token of a receptionist of clinic 2 (isolation checks)
# @name foreignLogin
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/medicitas/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=medicitas-cli&username=diego.araya@heredia.medicitas.test&password={{$processEnv MEDICITAS_DEMO_USER_PASSWORD}}

@receptionist = {{receptionistLogin.response.body.access_token}}
@admin = {{adminLogin.response.body.access_token}}
@foreign = {{foreignLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 4. Who am I (tenant taken from the token)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{receptionist}}

### 5. 401 — no token
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/patients

### 6. 403 — receptionist on the audit log (clinic admin only, RF19)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/audit-log
Authorization: Bearer {{receptionist}}

### 7. RF7 availability (repeat it: X-Cache MISS → HIT)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/availability?professionalId={{professionalId}}&serviceId={{serviceId}}&date={{date}}
Authorization: Bearer {{receptionist}}

### 8. RF8 availability by service over a range (max 14 days)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/availability/search?serviceId={{serviceId}}&from={{date}}&to=2026-12-07
Authorization: Bearer {{receptionist}}

### 9. RF14 register a patient
# @name patient
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{receptionist}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identificationType": "passport",
  "identificationNumber": "HTTP-{{$randomInt 100000 999999}}",
  "firstName": "Lucía",
  "lastName": "Colección",
  "birthDate": "1988-07-14",
  "contact": { "email": "lucia@example.test", "phone": "+50688881234" }
}

@patientId = {{patient.response.body.data.patientId}}

### 10. RF9 book (use a startAt returned by request 7) — 201 / 409 SLOT_TAKEN / 400-422-404
# @name booking
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{receptionist}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-collection-{{$guid}}

{
  "patient": { "id": "{{patientId}}" },
  "professionalId": "{{professionalId}}",
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "startAt": "{{date}}T08:00:00-06:00"
}

@appointmentId = {{booking.response.body.data.appointmentId}}

### 11. RF10 reschedule (atomic)
# @name reschedule
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/appointments/{{appointmentId}}/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{receptionist}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startAt": "{{date}}T09:00:00-06:00" }

@currentId = {{reschedule.response.body.data.current.appointmentId}}

### 12. RF13 invalid transition: cancel the rescheduled (final) appointment → 409
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/appointments/{{appointmentId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{receptionist}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "invalid on purpose" }

### 13. RF12 outcome before the start time → 422 OUTCOME_BEFORE_START
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/appointments/{{currentId}}/outcome
Authorization: Bearer {{receptionist}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "outcome": "attended" }

### 14. RF11 cancel with reason
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/appointments/{{currentId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{receptionist}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Patient asked to cancel" }

### 15. RF16 history of the patient
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/patients/{{patientId}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{receptionist}}

### 16. RF20 clinic-wide agenda of the day
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/agenda?date={{date}}
Authorization: Bearer {{receptionist}}

### 17. RF21 counts by status
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/reports/appointment-status-counts?from={{date}}&to={{date}}
Authorization: Bearer {{receptionist}}

### 18. RF19 audit log of the patient (contact read/write entries)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/audit-log?patientId={{patientId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### 19. I5 — clinic 2 asks for the clinic-1 patient → 404
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/patients/{{patientId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{foreign}}
X-Tenant-Id: 10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

### 20. I5 — a tenant id smuggled in the query string → 400
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/patients?tenantId=10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{foreign}}
